\title{Moons Cluster Task Generator}
\description{
A \link[mlr3:TaskGenerator]{TaskGenerator} for two interleaving half circles ("moons"), in the spirit of
\code{sklearn.datasets.make_moons()}.
The \code{n} observations are split evenly between an upper half circle centered at the origin and a lower half circle
shifted to the right and down so that the two arcs interleave.
Each observation is perturbed with Gaussian noise of standard deviation \code{sd}.
The generated \link{TaskClust} only contains the numeric features \code{x1} and \code{x2}; the cluster membership is not
stored in the task.
The parameter \code{sd} is initialized to \code{0.1}.

The clusters are not convex, which makes this generator a standard test case for density-based and
connectivity-based methods such as DBSCAN, single linkage or spectral clustering, where centroid-based methods
such as k-means fail.
}
